Spring Actuator

Spring actuator is a module in the Spring Boot that helps you monitor and manage your application in production.
Its a built-in health and diagnostic toolkit for your app.
------------------------
What does spring actuator do?
It exposes production ready endpoints that give insights like:
- Application health
- Metrics (CPU, memory, requests)
- Environment properties.
- Logs
- Beans and mappings
------------------------
How to enable Actuator??
<dependency>
    <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>
    <artifactId>spring-boot-starter-actuator</artifactId>
</dependency>

Enable endpoints:
By default health is exposed.

To expose more
Properties:
management.endpoints.web.exposure.include=*

or specific ones:
management.endpoints.web.exposure.include=health,infor,metrics
------------------------
Access via browser:
http://localhot:8080/actuator

actuator/health check if app is running.
actuator/metrics performance data.
actuator/info Custom app info.
actuator/info Environment variables.
actuator/beans All spring beans
actuator/loggers Change log levels at runtime
